---
title: Roasted branzino
tags: [grill]
source: Roasted Branzino by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/roasted-branzino-2
---

== Chile butter ==

Melt the @butter{4%tbsp} with the @Calabrian chili{2%tbsp}(puréed) in a #sauté pan{} over medium-low heat, stirring until smooth. Off the heat, season with the juice of a @Meyer lemon{}, then keep warm over low heat.

== Fish ==

Heat a #grill{} to 500°F.

Salt the flesh side of the @branzino{1 1/2%lb}(whole, dry-aged, butterflied) well and leave ~{15%minutes}.

Grill skin side down ~{3%minutes}, until the skin is crisp. Turn and cook ~{2%minutes} more.

Plate skin side up. Scatter over @parsley{}, @dill{} and @oregano{}(leaves), and the @Fresno chile{}(thinly sliced).

Pour the chile butter over and finish with @extra virgin olive oil{}, @salt{} and @ground black pepper{}.
